# scoop export on Windows can emit CRLF; force LF for diff stability.
# See ADR 0019 (record-only) + ADR 0030 (per-host dump/<host>/ layout).
dump/*/scoop.json text eol=lf
# `just dump-skills-lock` rewrites the skill declaration; same LF pin.
dump/harness/skill-lock.json text eol=lf

# `just portless-doc` generates this (LF); `just portless-doc-check` verifies it
# with a raw `diff` in `ci`. Pin LF so a Windows checkout does not introduce CRLF
# and report the doc stale even though the committed blob is LF. Same rationale
# as dump/scoop.json above.
docs/portless-urls.md text eol=lf

# Shell scripts must be LF on every platform: shellcheck reads the working
# tree and treats CR as SC1017 error, breaking `just lint` and the
# test_install_sh_passes_shellcheck test on Windows hosts where
# core.autocrlf=true would otherwise convert the working tree to CRLF.
# See ADR 0020.
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf

# Go sources must be LF for the same reason: gofmt / gofumpt — reached through
# `golangci-lint run` and `golangci-lint fmt --diff` in `go-lint` — report a
# CRLF working tree as "File is not properly formatted". With core.autocrlf=true
# a Windows checkout fails `just check` on an untouched .go file while the
# committed blob is LF. A fresh clone needs nothing; an existing Windows
# checkout needs a forced re-checkout, because git skips stat-clean paths (see
# ADR 0050). Same shape as the *.sh pin above.
*.go   text eol=lf
